  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Initial 1.0.0-beta release\n\t\t\t- Provides foundational exception and advisory signaling for Release-mode packages.\n\t\t\t- Includes metadata attributes shared across IVSoftware NuGet packages.\n\t\t\t1.0.0-rc1\n\t\t\t- ADDED supported framework: netstandard2.0\n\t\t\tStable 1.0.0\n\t\t\t- added missing 'event' keyword to 'BeginThrowOrAdvise'\n\t\t\tBeta release 1.0.1\n\t\t\t- Added [Policy] and [PolicyEnforcement] attributes for declarative policy metadata.\n\t\t\t- Introduced ThrowPolicyException extension to route policy violations through canonical Throw/Advisory pathways.\n\t\t\t- Enforced non-[Flags] constraint for Policy enums to preserve atomic violation semantics.\n\t\t\t- No breaking changes.\n\t\t\tRelease Candidate 1.0.1\n\t\t\t- Fixed @throw polarity on ThrowFramework\n\t\t\t- Added [NotFlags] as an opt-in enforcement mechanism for enums that are intended for parsing by field name.\n\t\t\t- Added [Claim] attribute for linking ReadMe claims to unit tests.\n\t\t\t- Added Extension: ToStrongNamedFriendAssembly(this object)\n\t\t\t- ORIGIN: AppDomain TypeCache with basic features.\n\t\t\tStable 1.0.1\n\t\t\t- Added unit test coverage for the pesky @throw polarity on ThrowFramework.\n\t\t\t- Not Added: What isn't (and won't be) included is [IFTTT] which will be available canonically in IVSoftware.Portable.Xml.Linq.Collections.",
